# state: any   (the golden cc9b4ced4a0f holds pathfind's profile; lane.accuracy804, #804)
# RalliSport Challenge (4D53000F): pathfind's recorded menu path (main menu RIGHT -> SINGLE RACE
# -> Rally -> Safari SS1 -> default car -> start race), then hands off the pad. flicker801's
# positive bursts came from this mode; rallisport-804.route took CAREER (Safari Trophy) to the
# same stage, and its run (1791136124-lane.accuracy804-3752333) had no rival in view at any
# race clock from 7.37 to 46.30.
#
# Fixed waits only (a dispatched soak gets the route's text; a `waitfor` crop does not travel).
# Times are route-relative, from the first run's log (each `wait 6` + shot took 6.3-7.4 s):
#   0-64 s no input; START at ~+64 (title by ~+70); title A ~+73; profile A ~+79 -> main menu.
#   main menu: RIGHT on the hat (Single Race; Career is lit), A ~+89 -> race type (Rally lit) A ~+95 ->
#   track (SAFARI SS1 lit) A ~+102 -> car (default lit) A ~+108 -> loading 25 s -> options,
#   "start race" lit, A ~+134. The first run's race clock read 0 seven seconds after this A,
#   so race clock 0 is ~+141 and the rival stretch (race clock ~7.5 s on) ~+148.
#   The second A at ~+142 is a spare for a lost press; in a running race A does nothing visible.
#   A lost RIGHT sends the A presses down Career's path instead (shots `racetype`/`track` say so).
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
press START
wait 5
shot title
wait 3
press A
wait 6
press A
wait 6
shot mainmenu
# RIGHT as pathfind sends it (pathfind.py send(): HATX max, then mid, 0.35 s), not `press RIGHT`
# (pad.sh's BTN_DPAD_RIGHT key, which goldeneye-ra.first-run.route found ignored by a title).
axis HATX max
wait 0.35
axis HATX mid
wait 2
press A
wait 6
shot racetype
press A
wait 6
shot track
press A
wait 6
shot car
press A
wait 25
shot options
press A
wait 8
press A
wait 3
shot r1
wait 2
shot r2
wait 2
shot r3
wait 2
shot r4
wait 2
shot r5
wait 3
shot r6
wait 3
shot r7
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    wait 20
    shot hold
}
